sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 6, docs/reference/development-containers.md#copy-a-feature): the `--from` path of `instance:create` on a container Node. Only the steps that `--from` adds or changes are drawn; the rest is container/create.mmd. Files come from the source container, the branch from the source Instance's HEAD, the data from a dump of its database. The source keeps running and is never paused.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:create --from
  %% kind: instance.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as New container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:create --from<br/>PROJECT NODE NAME
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:create PROJECT NODE NAME --from=INSTANCE`
  %%> - syntax: `<project> <node> <name> --from=<instance> [--branch=BRANCH] [--root=PATH] [--domain=HOST]`
  Note over GW: Check the source<br/>same Project · same Node
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the source is an active container Instance of the same Project on the same Node, else `instance.source_not_container`
  %%> - its database is on the Node's database server; the new database goes to the same server
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Instance is reserved as in create; the intent names the source's container and database
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-create
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  SW->>N: Read the source commit<br/>git rev-parse HEAD
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus exec` into the source container: reads the commit that `HEAD` points to, as `agent`; local commits count, uncommitted files do not
  %%> - bundles the history from that commit for the new container
  %%> Why no pause:
  %%> - the files of the copy come from the source container, which never changes, so nothing in the source needs to stop
  SW->>C: Copy source container<br/>Ansible · tags container
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same step as in create, from `<project>-source`
  %%> - pushes the bundle in and creates the branch at the source commit; `--branch` names it, else the Instance name
  SW->>N: Dump the source database<br/>pg_dump · one snapshot
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `pg_dump` in custom format; PostgreSQL reads one consistent snapshot while the source keeps writing
  %%> - the dump stays on the Node, readable by root only, and is removed at the end of the run
  %%> Runs beside the step before it: Swamp starts both at once.
  SW->>N: Restore into new database<br/>pg_restore · one transaction
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Orbit creates the owner and database first; the restore uses `--no-owner --no-privileges --single-transaction --exit-on-error` into the empty database
  %%> - roles and grants come from Orbit, never from the dump
  %%> Side effects:
  %%> - copied jobs and mail settings come with the data; the Project's setup steps run before any Process starts, so a Project clears what it must not repeat there (open question 6 in the plan)
  SW->>C: Prepare, start, set up<br/>as in create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the workspace, the first start of T3, the setup steps as `orbit`, the Processes, the Route and the Gateway session, as in container/create.mmd
  alt all steps pass in budget
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record Instance, T3 server<br/>active · registered
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Instance records its source Instance and source commit
  else a step fails or the budget ends
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    %%> What stays:
    %%> - the stopped container and its database; the source was never touched
    Note over GW: Record the failure
  end
